The `content` package: portable document content
=================================================

A region whose value is `Content` becomes structure in the output: emphasis, links, images, tables, code. Each
backend writes it in its own syntax (`lamlet build`). Content is a flat list of events, so Lamlet code can build,
join, and transform it with ordinary list functions; the Rust side turns the events into a tree and checks that
every opening has its closing.

$[Import* std]

1. Types

An attribute of an element: a key and its value as text.

$[# Attr [% {Struct {' {Field "key" String} {Field "value" String}}}]]

An element's name and attributes.

$[# Element [% {Struct {' {Field "name" String} {Field "attrs" {List Attr}}}}]]

One event: the opening of an element, its closing (by name), text, or a leaf element with no children.

$[# Event [% {Variant {' {Field "open" Element} {Field "close" String} {Field "text" String} {Field "leaf" Element}}}]]

Content: a list of events. Lists of content join with `cat` (or std's `flatten`).

$[# Content [% {List Event}]]

2. Building blocks

$[# attr {^ {key value} {: {. key key value value} Attr}}]
$[# _el {^ {name attrs} {: {. name name attrs attrs} Element}}]
$[# _open {^ {name attrs} {: {#open {_el name attrs}} Event}}]
$[# _close {^ {name} {: {#close name} Event}}]
$[# _wrap {^ {name attrs body} {: {flatten {' {' {_open name attrs}} body {' {_close name}}}} Content}}]
$[# _leaf {^ {name attrs} {: {' {: {#leaf {_el name attrs}} Event}} Content}}]

Content from pieces of content, in order.

$[# cat {^ {parts} {: {flatten parts} Content}}]

Nothing.

$[# empty [% {: {'} Content}]]

3. Inlines

Text. Writers escape it for their format.

$[# text {^ {s} {: {' {: {#text s} Event}} Content}}]

Emphasis and strong emphasis, of a String or of content.

$[# emph {^ {s} {_wrap "emph" {'} {text s}}}]
$[# emphOf {^ {body} {_wrap "emph" {'} body}}]
$[# strong {^ {s} {_wrap "strong" {'} {text s}}}]
$[# strongOf {^ {body} {_wrap "strong" {'} body}}]

A link with a String label, or with content.

$[# link {^ {label href} {_wrap "link" {' {attr "href" href}} {text label}}}]
$[# linkOf {^ {body href} {_wrap "link" {' {attr "href" href}} body}}]

An image, with its alternative text, and optionally a title.

$[# image {^ {src alt} {_leaf "image" {' {attr "src" src} {attr "alt" alt}}}}]
$[# imageTitled {^ {src alt title} {_leaf "image" {' {attr "src" src} {attr "alt" alt} {attr "title" title}}}}]

Code inside a line.

$[# code {^ {s} {_leaf "code" {' {attr "text" s}}}}]

A formula in TeX, inline or displayed.

$[# math {^ {tex} {_leaf "math" {' {attr "tex" tex}}}}]
$[# displayMath {^ {tex} {_leaf "math" {' {attr "tex" tex} {attr "display" "true"}}}}]

A line break.

$[# lineBreak [% {_leaf "break" {'}}]]

Markup for one format, copied unescaped by that format's backend and refused by the others: inline, or as a
block.

$[# raw {^ {format s} {_leaf "raw" {' {attr "format" format} {attr "text" s}}}}]
$[# rawBlock {^ {format s} {_leaf "rawBlock" {' {attr "format" format} {attr "text" s}}}}]

A named span with attributes, for hosts: a class in HTML, a cue for a narrated document. Writers that do not know
the name write only its content.

$[# span {^ {name attrs body} {_wrap "span" {cons {attr "name" name} attrs} body}}]

4. Blocks

A paragraph.

$[# paragraph {^ {body} {_wrap "paragraph" {'} body}}]

A heading of level 1 to 6, from a String; `headingId` also gives it an id (a speech section, an HTML anchor).

$[# heading {^ {level s} {_wrap "heading" {' {attr "level" {str level}}} {text s}}}]
$[# headingId {^ {level id s} {_wrap "heading" {' {attr "level" {str level}} {attr "id" id}} {text s}}}]
$[# headingOf {^ {level id body} {_wrap "heading" {' {attr "level" {str level}} {attr "id" id}} body}}]

Lists of items, each item content.

$[# _items {^ {items} {flatten {map items {^ {c} {_wrap "item" {'} c}}}}}]
$[# bullets {^ {items} {_wrap "list" {'} {_items items}}}]
$[# numbered {^ {items} {_wrap "list" {' {attr "ordered" "true"}} {_items items}}}]

Lists of Strings, as bullets or numbered.

$[# bulletsOf {^ {items} {bullets {map items text}}}]
$[# numberedOf {^ {items} {numbered {map items text}}}]

A table from a header row and rows of Strings, or of content.

$[# _cells {^ {row} {flatten {map row {^ {c} {_wrap "cell" {'} c}}}}}]
$[# tableOf {^ {header rows}
    {_wrap "table" {'} {flatten {cons {_wrap "head" {'} {_cells header}} {map rows {^ {r} {_wrap "row" {'} {_cells r}}}}}}}}]
$[# table {^ {header rows} {tableOf {map header text} {map rows {^ {r} {map r text}}}}}]

A block of code in a language (`""` for none).

$[# codeBlock {^ {lang s} {_leaf "codeBlock" {' {attr "lang" lang} {attr "text" s}}}}]

A named group of blocks with attributes, for hosts, like `span` for inlines.

$[# group {^ {name attrs body} {_wrap "group" {cons {attr "name" name} attrs} body}}]

5. Speech

Shown as `shown` and spoken as `spoken`: a formula, a code name, an abbreviation.

$[# say {^ {shown spoken} {_wrap "say" {' {attr "spoken" spoken}} shown}}]

A named point between words, with attributes, that a speech host times to the next spoken word.

$[# anchor {^ {name attrs} {_leaf "anchor" {cons {attr "name" name} attrs}}}]

Silence, in seconds.

$[# pause {^ {seconds} {_leaf "pause" {' {attr "seconds" {str seconds}}}}}]
